#!/bin/bash
# FROM-SCRATCH, AUGMENTED-SUBSET arm CE-sub: train MViTv2-S with RANDOM INIT on the
# 6,000 ASL-Citizen train originals that HAVE Flux augmentations. 450-way task.
#
# WHY: in the full-set aug experiment only 6,000 / 40,154 originals (15%) carry augs,
# so any aug effect is diluted across 2,731 glosses. Here the SAME 6,000 parents are
# the entire training set, so the paired arm (scratch_asl_sub450_aug.job) has 100%
# augmentation coverage. CE-sub is its no-aug control. Tests whether the full-set
# aug null is a coverage-dilution artifact.
#
# The 6,000 parents cover exactly 450 of the 2,731 glosses at 5-18 parents/gloss
# (median 14) vs the full set's 9-24 (median 15) -> per-gloss density is matched;
# the TASK SIZE is not (450-way vs 2,731-way). That confound is acknowledged.
#
# Random-init mechanism (empty backbone-key-less checkpoint) is unchanged from
# scratch_asl_citizen_ce.job -- see that file's header and scratch-baseline-prep.md.
#
# LABEL SPACE (450-way):
#   train_logos_asl_citizen.py builds gloss_to_idx = sorted(set(glosses)) from
#   args.train_csv.replace("splits_aug","splits"). For this arm that is this file's
#   own train.csv -> 450 glosses, indices 0..449. The head width is a SEPARATE flag
#   (--num_classes, default 2731) and MUST be passed as 450, which it is below.
#   ClipDataset drops rows whose gloss is outside gloss_to_idx, and val.csv/test.csv
#   in splits_sub450/ are already filtered to the same 450 glosses.

#SBATCH --partition=gpu_a100
#SBATCH --gpus=1
#SBATCH --job-name=sub450_ce
#SBATCH --ntasks=1
#SBATCH --cpus-per-task=16
#SBATCH --time=10:00:00              # est. 6.8 GPU-h (20 ep x 6,000 clips = 4.1 h at the
                                     # MEASURED 0.124 s/clip of job 24985151, + 2.7 h
                                     # full-dataset feature extract). Limit also caps
                                     # spend at 1,280 SBU.
#SBATCH --output=/home/psobecki/fork_mmaction2/jobs/output/slurm_%x_%A.txt

module purge
module load 2025
cd $HOME/fork_mmaction2
source .venv/bin/activate
export PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1

# ── run config (identical to scratch_asl_citizen_ce.job EXCEPT epochs, see note) ──
TAG=sub450_ce
UNFREEZE=16          # full network — mandatory for random init
LR=1e-3              # SAME as the full-size template
LLRD=1.0
BATCH=6
GRAD_ACCUM=4         # effective batch 24
EPOCHS=20            # DEVIATION from the template's 30. The full-size runs measured
                     # 0.124 s/clip (5,220 opt-steps in 4:18:35, job 24985151), ~1.5x
                     # slower than the 0.9 GPU-h/epoch the prep artifact assumed. At 30
                     # epochs the CE-sub + AUG-sub pair costs ~5,490 SBU, over the 4,500
                     # hard cap. 20 epochs keeps the pair at ~3,850 SBU. BOTH sub450 arms
                     # use 20, so the CE-sub vs AUG-sub contrast (the primary one) stays
                     # exactly matched; only the sub-vs-full epoch count differs.
NUM_CLASSES=450      # 450-way head — the subset covers 450 of the 2,731 glosses

SPLITS=$HOME/ASL_Citizen/splits_sub450

VIDEO_DIR=/scratch-shared/psobecki/ASL_Citizen/videos
SAVE_DIR=/scratch-shared/psobecki/runs/asl_ft_${TAG}
FEAT_DIR=/scratch-shared/psobecki/ASL_Citizen/logos_features_${TAG}
LOGFILE=/home/psobecki/fork_mmaction2/jobs/output/slurm_${SLURM_JOB_NAME}_${SLURM_JOB_ID}.txt

# ── pre-flight: splits must be the expected size / gloss space ───────────────
for f in train val test; do
    [ -f "$SPLITS/$f.csv" ] || { echo "FATAL: missing $SPLITS/$f.csv"; exit 1; }
done
NTRAIN=$(($(wc -l < $SPLITS/train.csv) - 1))
NGLOSS=$(tail -n +2 $SPLITS/train.csv | cut -d, -f3 | sort -u | wc -l)
echo "[pre-flight] train rows=$NTRAIN (expect 6000)  glosses=$NGLOSS (expect 450)"
[ "$NTRAIN" -eq 6000 ] || { echo "FATAL: train.csv is $NTRAIN rows, expected 6000"; exit 1; }
[ "$NGLOSS" -eq 450 ]  || { echo "FATAL: train.csv has $NGLOSS glosses, expected 450"; exit 1; }

# ── synthesise the empty (backbone-key-less) checkpoint for random init ───────
EMPTY_CKPT=$HOME/fork_mmaction2/data/model/EMPTY_random_init.pth
if [ ! -f "$EMPTY_CKPT" ]; then
    python -c "import torch, os; os.makedirs(os.path.dirname('$EMPTY_CKPT'), exist_ok=True); torch.save({'state_dict': {}}, '$EMPTY_CKPT')"
    echo "[random-init] wrote empty checkpoint $EMPTY_CKPT (loads no weights)"
fi

# ── train (random init, 6,000 parent originals, 450-way) ─────────────────────
srun python train_logos_asl_citizen.py \
    --train_csv  $SPLITS/train.csv \
    --video_dir  $VIDEO_DIR \
    --checkpoint $EMPTY_CKPT \
    --save_dir   $SAVE_DIR \
    --num_classes $NUM_CLASSES \
    --unfreeze_blocks $UNFREEZE --llrd $LLRD \
    --epochs $EPOCHS --batch_size $BATCH --grad_accum $GRAD_ACCUM --lr $LR \
    --workers 16 \
    --mlflow --mlflow_run_name asl_ft_${TAG} --slurm_log "$LOGFILE" \
    --val_csv $SPLITS/val.csv

# ── re-extract all videos with the from-scratch checkpoint (Eval A + Eval B) ─
# Kept identical to the full-size templates (all 83,399 videos) so the feature dirs
# stay comparable with every other run. Eval must use splits_sub450/test.csv.
srun python extract_logos_features.py \
    --video_dir   $VIDEO_DIR \
    --output_dir  $FEAT_DIR \
    --checkpoint  $SAVE_DIR/checkpoint_best.pt \
    --dataset_name asl_citizen \
    --preproc logos_native --overwrite \
    --workers 16 --batch_size 8

echo "Done. Features in $FEAT_DIR — eval with eval_asl_citizen_features.job (MMPT venv, genoa),"
echo "pointed at $SPLITS/test.csv (450-gloss subset), NOT the full test split."

RUNID=$(cat $SAVE_DIR/mlflow_run_id.txt 2>/dev/null)
[ -n "$RUNID" ] && python mlflow_log_slurm_log.py "$RUNID" "$LOGFILE" || true
